\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(int)\b numberOfRowsInTableView:\b0 (NSTableView\'80*)\i aTableView\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns the number of records managed for \i aTableView\i0  by the data source object. An NSTableView uses this method to determine how many rows it should create and display.\
\fs14\
\fs46\
\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s43 \li1512 \fi-503 \ri1007 \ql \tx1512 \tx8265 \f5 \b0 \fs52 p\tab \f0 \b \fs28 {{\NeXTHelpMarker5423 \markername NS_DEV_DOCFOR:objc_method:[NSTableDataSource-tableView:objectValueForTableColumn:row:];}
¬}\pard \s43 \li1512 \fi-503 \ri1007 \ql \tx1512 \tx8265 tableView:objectValueForTableColumn:row:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(id)\b tableView:\b0 (NSTableView\'80*)\i aTableView\
\fi0 \b \i0 objectValueForTableColumn:\b0 (NSTableColumn\'80*)\i aTableColumn\
\fi0 \b \i0 row:\b0 (int)\i rowIndex\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns an attribute value for the record in \i aTableView\i0  at \i rowIndex\i0 . \i aTableColumn\i0  contains the identifier for the attribute, which you get by using NSTableColumn\'27s \b identifier\b0  method. For example, if \i aTableColumn\i0  stands for the city that an employee lives in and \i rowIndex\i0  specifies the record for an employee who lives in Portland, this method returns an object with a string value of \'aaPortland\'ba. See the category description for an example.\
\fs14\
